<title>UK: British Energy April output sales rise.</title>
<headline>British Energy April output sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nuclear electricity producer British Energy Plc said on Tuesday that total sales reached 5.79 Terawatt hours (TWh) in April from 5.70 a year ago.</p>
<p>A Terawatt hour is the largest unit of measurement for electricity sales, representing one billion kilowatt hours.</p>
<p>The following table details sales from each power station in TWh. Comparisons are with April 1996:</p>
<p>    Station		   (April 96)	   (April 97)</p>
<p>    Hinkley Point B	  0.88		   0.82</p>
<p>    Hunterston B	     0.51		   0.83</p>
<p>    Dungeness B		0.57		   0.60</p>
<p>    Heysham 1		  0.46		   0.62</p>
<p>    Hartlepool		 0.79		   0.60</p>
<p>    Torness		    0.87		   0.66</p>
<p>    Heysham 2		  0.76		   0.80</p>
<p>    Sizewell B		 0.86		   0.86</p>
<p>    Total			5.70		   5.79</p>
<p>April is the first month of British Energy's accounting year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
